  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 94872708bfe9e4851981e9e1837f1ac3, type: 3}
  m_Name: HydriaVase
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: Hydria Apothecary Vase
  description: 'A hydria-type apothecary maiolica vase created in Savona (Italy)
    in the late 17th century. Handles in the shape of (fantastic) animal heads on
    massive bent necks. At the front, towards the bottom of the vase, a gargoyle
    in relief. Plugged with regular cork, its mouth doubles as an opening for pouring
    out the contents of the vase. Smaller gargoyles, without any openings, located
    under the handles, alongside the vase. At the front, above an inscription, a
    hand-painted decoration: a human figure keeping a two-headed dragon on a leash.
    A centaur slaying a dragon adorns the back of the vase.'
  audio: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4c4ec27744ffcb046a04e84227fe33c5, type: 3}
